The FINALPLAY16 Vulkan bridge inherited the bring-up diagnostics used while the
32-to-64-bit graphics-pipeline layout was being established.  They printed and
flushed large structure dumps from vkCreateGraphicsPipelines and also logged
descriptor layouts, render passes and shader modules unconditionally.  That is
the same first-use path being measured for scene and enemy hitches.

Make all bridge diagnostics default-off.  MGS2_BOX86_VK_DIAG=1 restores the
bounded first-512 pipeline dump and enables the existing DMC3_VK_* diagnostic
knobs.  The ordinary path retains the same structure alignment and native
Vulkan calls and performs only one cached atomic flag read per intercepted
creation call.

